{"slug":"brian-higgins","qid":"Q505581","name":"Brian Higgins","desc":"U.S. Representative from New York","article":"Brian Higgins","born":"1959-10-06","died":null,"birthplace":"Buffalo","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-26","f":2013,"u":2025},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-27","f":2005,"u":2013},{"t":"New York State Assembly","w":"","f":1999,"u":2004}],"summary":"Brian Michael Higgins (born October 6, 1959) is an American former politician who was the U.S. representative for New York's 26th congressional district, from 2005 until 2024. The district, numbered as the 27th district from 2005 to 2013 and as the 26th from 2013 to 2024, included Buffalo and Niagara Falls, along with some surrounding urban and suburban areas. Higgins is a member of the Democratic Party, and of several congressional committees and caucuses.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":156883,"s":63.94,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":223366,"s":69.81,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":169166,"s":73.34,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":215289,"s":74.58,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":113210,"s":68.15,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"NY-26","p":"D","v":212588,"s":74.79,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"NY-27","p":"D","v":119085,"s":60.94,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgings"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"NY-27","p":"D","v":185713,"s":74.42,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"NY-27","p":"D","v":140027,"s":79.27,"w":true,"n":"Brian Higgins"},{"y":2004,"o":"H","k":"NY-27","p":"D","v":143332,"s":50.67,"w":true,"n":"Brian M Higgins"}]}